
[5] LOCAL VISCOSITY  (measured pore width w = 5.00 sigma, NARROW)
    in-pore density: mean 0.845, pore-centre 0.868 (target rho* = 0.8)
    rho_m(z) shows 4 wall-induced layer(s) across the pore - no bulk region.
    eta(z) = -P_xz/(dvx/dz) has NO single plateau here: a local Newtonian viscosity
    no longer describes the liquid (Travis, Todd & Evans 1997).
